--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8ef4a382a350f98438c21cfd3c789fdf, type: 3}
  m_Name: Eyes
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonTitle: Eyes
  lessonId: eyes
  slides:
  - slideName: Slide 1
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Welcome to Life and Death! In this section, you'll learn how to sustain
      or capture large groups of stones.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 2
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Let's start with the basics first. This shape is called an "eye" because
      white cannot play at the highlighted spot. Moves that places stones at a spot
      causes it to have zero liberties are illegal moves.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 3
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Therefore, if white wants to capture this, it'll have to fully surround
      it. This move no longer is illegal because the capture allows it to gain liberties.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 4
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: These all count as "real" eyes because white would need to fully surround
      them to capture.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 5
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: However, these are "fake" eyes because white does not need to fully
      surround them to capture a part of them. Just remember that if it is  missing
      more than two corners (one corner if on the side), it is fake.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 6
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: There are also big eyes. They surround two spaces instead of one.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 7
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: If white wants to capture one, it may try to place stones in the eye,
      but after placing the first, it cannot place the second because it becomes
      a illegal move (causes 0 liberties).
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 8
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: It'll still have to surround it fully to capture.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 9
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Want to make a group of stones immortal? Well, you can now with eyes!
      Notice how this group of black stones has two eyes?
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 10
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Because it has two, white can now never capture this group because
      both spots are illegal moves.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 11
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Having more eyes is fine. As long as it has two or more eyes and is
      connected, it cannot be captured.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 12
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Now it's your turn. Save your stones by making two eyes!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 2c0e829b4c5453148a84bfff9c7779c1, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 13
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Save your stones by making two eyes!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 4c2495fb715833a4d88ebaf255b78559, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 14
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Save your stones by making two eyes!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 20ee8890e9499df4ca75e256ed1b271b, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 15
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Great job this lesson. Come back next time to learn more abot life
      and death!
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
